      "topic": "pk-punjab/xi/chemistry/c11-chem/ch6/6.12.1",
      "title": "6.12.1 Calculating ΔG° for a reaction",
      "language": "en",
      "source_refs": [
        {
          "source_document_id": "b07b1f6c-f5a4-509d-ae86-73be5bffb0d4",
          "pdf_from": 139,
          "pdf_to": 140,
          "note": "Topic 6.12.1, printed pages 139-140; Sample Problems 6.12 and 6.13 (the print has no 6.10 or 6.11). The chapter exercise (pages 140-143) is not reproduced."
        }
      ],
      "body": {
        "blocks": [
          {
            "type": "heading",
            "level": 4,
            "text": "Sample Problem 6.12",
            "book_errors": [
              "Sample Problem 6.12"
            ]
          },
          {
            "type": "paragraph",
            "text": "For the reaction:"
          },
          {
            "type": "paragraph",
            "text": "CaSO₄(s) → Ca²⁺(aq) + SO₄²⁻(aq)"
          },
          {
            "type": "paragraph",
            "text": "Calculate ΔH°, ΔS° and ΔG° at 25 °C using the following data; and discuss its spontaneity."
          },
          {
            "type": "paragraph",
            "text": "Heat of Formation: ΔH°f [CaSO₄(s)] = -1432.7 kJ, ΔH°f [Ca²⁺(aq)] = -543.0 kJ, ΔH°f [SO₄²⁻(aq)] = -907.5 kJ"
          },
          {
            "type": "paragraph",
            "text": "Standard entropy: S°[CaSO₄(s)] = 106.7 J/K, S°[Ca²⁺(aq)] = –55.2 J/K, S°[SO₄²⁻(aq)] = +17.2 J/K"
          },
          {
            "type": "paragraph",
            "text": "Solution",
            "bold": [
              "Solution"
            ]
          },
          {
            "type": "paragraph",
            "text": "ΔH° = ∑ ΔHf (products) – ∑ ΔHf (reactants) = [–543.0 –907.5] – [–1432.7] = –17.8 kJ",
            "bold": [
              "–17.8 kJ"
            ]
          },
          {
            "type": "paragraph",
            "text": "ΔS° = ∑S°(products) – ∑S°(reactants) = [(–55.2 + 17.2) – (106.7)] J/K = –1447 J/K",
            "book_errors": [
              "= –1447 J/K"
            ]
          },
          {
            "type": "paragraph",
            "text": "ΔS° = –0.1447 kJ/K",
            "bold": [
              "–0.1447 kJ/K"
            ]
          },
          {
            "type": "paragraph",
            "text": "ΔG° = ΔH° – T ΔS° = (–17.8 kJ) – (298 K) × (–0.1447 kJ/K) = + 25.3 kJ",
            "bold": [
              "+ 25.3 kJ"
            ]
          },
          {
            "type": "paragraph",
            "text": "Result: We conclude that this process is nonspontaneous at standard conditions at 25 °C",
            "bold": [
              "Result:"
            ]
          },
          {
            "type": "callout",
            "tone": "correction",
            "title": "Book correction",
            "text": "(–55.2 + 17.2) – 106.7 = –144.7 J/K, not –1447 J/K; the book itself continues with –0.1447 kJ/K, so ΔG° = +25.3 kJ is right. The numbering is also a slip: the print goes from Sample problem 6.9 to 6.12, with no 6.10 or 6.11; nothing is missing."
          },
          {
            "type": "heading",
            "level": 4,
            "text": "Sample Problem 6.13"
          },
          {
            "type": "paragraph",
            "text": "What is the standard free-energy, ΔG° for the following reaction (Haber’s process) at 25°C?"
          },
          {
            "type": "paragraph",
            "text": "N₂(g) + 3 H₂(g) → 2 NH₃(g)"
          },
          {
            "type": "paragraph",
            "text": "Also discuss its spontaneity."
          },
          {
            "type": "paragraph",
            "text": "Heat of Formation: ΔH°f [N₂(g)] = 0 kJ, ΔH°f [H₂(g)] = 0 kJ, ΔH°f [NH₃(g)] = –45.9 kJ"
          },
          {
            "type": "paragraph",
            "text": "Standard entropy: S°[N₂(g)] = 191.5 J/K, S°[H₂(g)] = 130.6 J/K, S°[NH₃(g)] = +193 J/K"
          },
          {
            "type": "paragraph",
            "text": "Solution",
            "bold": [
              "Solution"
            ]
          },
          {
            "type": "paragraph",
            "text": "ΔH° = ∑ ΔHf (products) – ∑ ΔHf (reactants) = [2 × (–45.9)] – [0 + 0] = –91.8 kJ",
            "bold": [
              "–91.8 kJ"
            ]
          },
          {
            "type": "paragraph",
            "text": "ΔS° = ∑nS°(products) – ∑mS°(reactants) = [2 × (193)] – [191.5 + 3 × 130.6] J/K = –197 J/K"
          },
          {
            "type": "paragraph",
            "text": "ΔS° = –0.197 kJ/K",
            "bold": [
              "–0.197 kJ/K"
            ]
          },
          {
            "type": "paragraph",
            "text": "ΔG° = ΔH° – T ΔS° = (–91.88 kJ) – (298 K) × (–0.197 kJ/K) = –33.1 kJ",
            "book_errors": [
              "(–91.88 kJ)"
            ]
          },
          {
            "type": "paragraph",
            "text": "Result",
            "bold": [
              "Result"
            ]
          },
          {
            "type": "paragraph",
            "text": "Since ΔG° is a negative value, thus it is concluded that Haber’s process is spontaneous at standard conditions , i.e. at 25 °C."
          },
          {
            "type": "callout",
            "tone": "correction",
            "title": "Book correction",
            "text": "ΔH° was found as –91.8 kJ, so the ΔG° line should use –91.8 kJ, not –91.88 kJ: ΔG° = –91.8 – 298 × (–0.197) = –33.1 kJ."
          }
        ]
      }
    }
  ]
}
